From 5490a3d55c182c0025aea4a6044652f2650b38ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 21:22:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: Split MT6789 CCCI SoC core from WWAN layer

Resolve the M2b upstream subsystem boundary by splitting the MediaTek
MT6789 CCCI modem stack cleanly along kernel subsystem lines:

- Move SoC modem power/EL3 SiP SMC boot, CCIF0 shared-memory ringbuffer
  transport, and RPC/FS/Audio mailbox services (mtk_ccci_core.c,
  mtk_ccci_ringbuf.c, mtk_ccci_rpc.c, mtk_ccci_fs.c, mtk_ccci_aud.c) into
  drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk_ccci/ (CONFIG_MTK_CCCI_SOC, mtk-ccci-soc).
- Export the shared transport and auxiliary-bus interface header at
  include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk_ccci.h with RCU-protected fast-path RX/IRQ
  ops and mutex-serialized lifecycle callbacks (mtk_ccci_register_wwan_ops,
  mtk_ccci_unregister_wwan_ops, and mtk_ccci_tx_send).
- Keep drivers/net/wwan/mtk_ccci/ (CONFIG_MTK_CCCI, mtk_ccci_wwan) strictly
  for the Linux WWAN AT control port and DPMAIF v1 + SMEM UL network data
  plane, bound via an auxiliary_bus child device (mtk_ccci_soc.wwan).
- Preserve all sysfs paths, /dev/ccci_{fs,rpc,aud}, /dev/wwan0at0, wwan0/1
  netdevs, and existing CONFIG_MTK_CCCI=y configs (selects MTK_CCCI_SOC).

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
